Subject: [PATCH] l10n: map the Nulavio branding directory for translations

Firefox's l10n configuration only maps the official branding directory.
Without this entry the multi-locale packaging step cannot find translated
Nulavio brand strings (it fails with MissingJarSource), and the only
alternative is shipping the brand's legal line in English to every locale.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not applicable (Nulavio-specific branding directory).
---
--- a/browser/locales/l10n.toml
+++ b/browser/locales/l10n.toml
@@ -133,6 +133,12 @@ locales = [
     reference = "browser/branding/official/locales/en-US/**"
     l10n = "{l}browser/branding/official/**"
 
+# Nulavio branding (translations ship in Nulavio's browser/l10n/, see
+# scripts/upstream/fetch_firefox_l10n.py).
+[[paths]]
+    reference = "browser/branding/nulavio/locales/en-US/**"
+    l10n = "{l}browser/branding/nulavio/**"
+
 # This file was removed in bug 1948916. In order to keep this file in
 # repositories, we need to preserve this entry until esr115 becomes
 # unsupported.
